;; M-wm-wiring — component map for the flight of a lifecycle mission
;; (first target M-autoclock-in). Author claude-10, 2026-09-25, DERIVE's first
;; artefact (WM-MAP-I). Checked by futon3c.diagramprover.wiring over futon2's
;; files at :futon2-sha, materialised from git into a temp root by
;; test/futon3c/diagramprover/wm_flight_wiring_test.clj (the registered run).
;;
;; REFERENT. The sites are the code that flies: flight/run! (flight.clj:246),
;; whose production caller is flight_driver.clj:123 under --run; each click is
;; a POST to /api/alpha/wm/click that runs the tick in
;; scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj. N0 checks each component site
;; against a registered load closure (test-registry-307b8969, the
;; mission-reading-c8-test run, which loads the flight and the tick). The
;; earlier holes/labs/M-diagramprover/wm-wiring.edn records how close the
;; paper map came to mapping the futon3c pilot peripheral instead of the
;; futon2 War Machine; this map names futon2 files only.
;;
;; FORM. One component box per inventory row (0-11 of M-wm-wiring), plus a
;; test box per row as its declared reader. A box declares the fields the
;; WIRED code will read and write, at var grain; where the code does not do so
;; yet, the checker's finding is the row's to-do, and :expected-findings in
;; the registered test lists them exactly. Wiring a row deletes its expected
;; findings in the same commit as the code. Keys are chosen to be distinctive
;; at their site: conformance is textual (it counts comments) and direction is
;; checked only under {:heuristic? true}.
;;
;; Components outside futon2 are siteless (exempt from conformance, still in
;; the graph): the W_c checker (futon3c holes/labs/M-futon-seams/exemplar/
;; proof2a_check.clj, warranted separately, test-registry-1757d974).
{:spec/id :wm-flight-wiring
 :repos {"futon2" "5c6acc21" "futon3c" "58f1a8cb"}
 ;; The owner's text is the one constraint (exogenous: nothing on the map
 ;; writes it); the spans that locate and pin it are observations of it.
 ;; Read by futon3c.diagramprover.ct-projection (296a08ca).
 :field-roles {:owner-text :constraint :want-span :observation :text-sha256 :observation}
 :boxes
 [;; ---- row 1, Clause T: target. The field exists, and the outer cascade (select) chooses among
  ;; its eligible targets; the loop entry's plan mode calls it (H-T-CALLER-I). Running a flight is not wired.
  {:box/id :r1-target-field :row 1 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/target_field.clj" :var "step"}
   :writes [:next-step]}
  {:box/id :r1-outer-cascade :row 1 :box/kind :component
   ;; BUILT (H-T-CALLER-I, futon2 b66369d3): select chooses among the field's
   ;; ELIGIBLE targets (feasibility as support), E uniform-no-data, G typed
   ;; absent, a seeded draw whose generator, seed, value and the excluded list
   ;; are on the record. It reads :eligible off the field's entries and
   ;; :trigger off its opts, and writes the choice. The reads below that it does
   ;; not make yet are the row's to-do (the E from the fold, the publication
   ;; and the clock lineage), findings until it reads them.
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/outer_cascade.clj" :var "select"}
   :reads [:trigger :next-step :eligible :pair-overlap :enactment-records :publication-observed
           :clock-lineage]
   :writes [:chosen-target :draw-seed :target-selection]}
  {:box/id :r1-test :row 1 :box/kind :test
   :site {:file "futon2/test/futon2/aif/outer_cascade_test.clj"}
   :reads [:draw-seed :chosen-target :target-selection]}

  ;; ---- row 2, Clause C: the read step. Components exist; the flight does not call them.
  {:box/id :r2-served-by-reading :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/served_by_reading.clj" :var "proposal"}
   :reads [:owner-text] :writes [:want-span :text-sha256]}
  {:box/id :r2-verifier :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/scripts/futon2/wm/extract_outcomes.clj" :var "verify-proposed-link"}
   :reads [:want-span :text-sha256]}
  {:box/id :r2-flight-read :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/flight_runner.clj" :var "read-fn"}
   ;; reads the flight's target as (:target flight), a keyword call the
   ;; prover's record scope does not yet attribute; the read step is where
   ;; the flight's :target lands once H9 lands (see :dispatch for why the
   ;; 1 -> 2 boundary carries no field today).
   ;; WM-HANDOFF-H9+H11-I: declared as a scoped read, [:target {:record
   ;; :flight}] (futon3c 16260b56 counts the keyword call on `flight`); its
   ;; writer is not yet attributable (see :flight-entry)
   :reads [:text-sha256 [:target {:record :flight}]]}
  ;; WM-HANDOFF-H1-I (WM-HANDOFFS-D H1): the flight loop, flight/run!, puts
  ;; the read step's result on the flight record as :readings (with
  ;; :before-click) and merges its :needs, and the ask step's :needs too; it
  ;; reads :needs back itself (the owner questions that end a flight before
  ;; a click, the pending asks). ONE WRITER: :needs has three textual
  ;; producers, read-fn's and ask-fn's return maps and run!'s merge; the box
  ;; is run!, and read-fn/ask-fn are returners whose maps run! merges (their
  ;; occurrences stand below), not declared writers. No row: run! is the
  ;; whole loop, no one clause's. The driver's summary (run-flight!) is the
  ;; reader of both after the flight. The read step does NOT hand the ask
  ;; step these fields: ask-fn reads neither; the read -> ask hand-off is the
  ;; interpretation store (reading/publish-*! in read-fn, reading/
  ;; published-* in flight/source-wants, which click-wants calls), not
  ;; boxed here
  {:box/id :flight-run :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/flight.clj" :var "run!"}
   ;; WM-HANDOFF-H9+H11-I: run! names the flight f: (:target f), scoped
   :record-aliases {:flight ["f"]}
   ;; F1a-1-I (futon2 d04711eb, 6165ec8b): the observation that followed an
   ;; enacted step, on its :enactments entry (flight/step-observation). Its
   ;; reader is F1b's step admission, not built: a to-do finding until then.
   :reads [:needs [:target {:record :flight}] :chosen :increment] :writes [:readings :needs [:observation {:record :enactment-entry}] [:step {:record :enactment-entry}]]}
  {:box/id :flight-ask-fn :box/kind :component
   ;; WM-HANDOFF-H9+H11-I: the ask step's (:target flight)
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/flight_runner.clj" :var "ask-fn"}
   :reads [[:target {:record :flight}]]}
  {:box/id :flight-driver-summary :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/flight_driver.clj" :var "run-flight!"}
   :reads [:readings :needs]}
  ;; WM-HANDOFF-H2-I (WM-HANDOFFS-D carrier 2): the read step's
  ;; publications reach the wants through the interpretation store
  ;; (<store>/<target>.edn, futon2/data/wm-interpretations). The store is a
  ;; carrier the map boxes by the functions that write and read its entries:
  ;; each published kind has ONE writer, its publish function in
  ;; futon2.aif.mission-reading (required as `reading`; read-fn calls it),
  ;; and one read-back function, called by flight/source-wants's :a-exits
  ;; method, which click-wants calls for the wants run! hands the ask step
  ;; (flight.clj :325-335). The fields are the store entry's keys, visible
  ;; at both sites. source-wants itself is not boxed: it is a defmulti, and
  ;; a var-grain site scans the defmulti form, not the :a-exits method; its
  ;; calls to the read-back functions are positional. The read-back boxes
  ;; sit in the ask step's lane: what they return is the ask step's input
  ;; (they are also read inside the read step, where read-fn asks
  ;; click-wants what readings are still needed)
  {:box/id :r2-store-criteria :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "publish-criteria!"}
   :writes [:criteria]}
  {:box/id :r2-store-coverage :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "publish-coverage!"}
   :writes [:coverage]}
  {:box/id :r2-store-locators :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "publish-locator!"}
   :writes [:locators]}
  {:box/id :r2-store-locator-questions :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "publish-locator-questions!"}
   :writes [:locator-questions]}
  {:box/id :r2-store-locator-declines :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "record-locator-decline!"}
   :writes [:locator-declines]}
  {:box/id :r2-store-constraints-read :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "publish-constraints!"}
   :writes [:constraints-read]}
  {:box/id :r3-store-criteria :row 3 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "published-criteria"}
   :reads [:criteria]}
  {:box/id :r3-store-coverage :row 3 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "published-coverage"}
   :reads [:coverage]}
  {:box/id :r3-store-locators :row 3 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "published-locators"}
   :reads [:locators]}
  {:box/id :r3-store-locator-questions :row 3 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "published-locator-questions"}
   :reads [:locator-questions]}
  {:box/id :r3-store-locator-declines :row 3 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "published-locator-declines"}
   :reads [:locator-declines]}
  {:box/id :r3-store-constraints-read :row 3 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/mission_reading.clj" :var "published-constraints"}
   :reads [:constraints-read]}
  ;; WM-NODE-R2-R3a-I (WM-SUPERSET-D sections 1-2): the tick's observation
  ;; and prediction error, in judge before the cascade assembly (obs/observe
  ;; at war_machine :6909, fe/channel-prediction-error at :7037, before
  ;; flight-assembly-input at :7247), so drawn first in lane 5.
  ;; r2-tick-observe: observation.clj/observe returns (with-meta values ...)
  ;; over a let-bound map keyed by channel (:loop-health, :stack-pct, ...);
  ;; every reader reads a channel under a variable key ((get obs channel),
  ;; (observation-status obs channel)), so no keyed field exists at either
  ;; end and none is declared. r3a-predict-observation: belief/
  ;; predict-observation returns a map keyed by channel, read the same way
  ;; ((get predictions ch), prediction-member's (get prediction k)): no
  ;; field. E4, R2 -> R3a (o): judge's local observation, bound to
  ;; (obs/observe scan-data) at :6909, is arg 1 of fe/channel-prediction-
  ;; error at :7037, whose first parameter obs is a plain symbol it reads
  ;; (channel-source-status obs channel); a whole-value positional hop,
  ;; declared with :passes (WM-PROVER-PASSES-I, futon3c 553d7edf) on
  ;; :r2-judge-observation (the caller, judge) into
  ;; :r3a-channel-prediction-error (the callee). The value is named
  ;; :tick-observation, a name the map gives the unkeyed observation (no
  ;; such key exists in the code; the :passes check is its occurrence)
  {:box/id :r2-tick-observe :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/observation.clj" :var "observe"}}
  {:box/id :r2-judge-observation :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj" :var "judge"}
   :writes [:tick-observation]
   :passes [{:value :tick-observation
             :from {:returns-of "obs/observe"}
             :to {:call "fe/channel-prediction-error" :arg 1
                  :callee-box :r3a-channel-prediction-error}}]}
  {:box/id :r3a-channel-prediction-error :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/free_energy.clj" :var "channel-prediction-error"}
   ;; WM-NODE-R1-I: E3's second callee (prediction, arg 3)
   :reads [:tick-observation :channel-prediction]}
  {:box/id :r3a-predict-observation :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/belief.clj" :var "predict-observation"}
   ;; WM-NODE-R1-I: E3's first callee (belief, arg 1); not declared, see
   ;; :r7-fold-call
   }
  {:box/id :r3a-prediction-error :box/kind :component
   ;; returns the prediction-error record, (merge stamp {:status :present
   ;; ... :error err :precision ... :weighted-error ...}) in each branch of
   ;; its trailing cond. :error already has a declared writer (the gate's
   ;; refusal), so the record's :error must be scoped [:error {:record
   ;; :prediction-error}]; with :returns-record :prediction-error the
   ;; scoped writes are :declaration-without-occurrence (checked): a
   ;; literal passed as merge's argument in return position is not
   ;; attributed. NEXT PROVER LIMIT: merge's literal arguments in return
   ;; position (as assoc's key-values already are). Until then no field is
   ;; declared here, and R7's (:error error-map) in weighted-error has no
   ;; attributable writer.
   ;; WM-NODE-R7-I: the limit is lifted (futon3c a35e5fbe, a literal
   ;; argument of a returned merge): declared, scoped
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/free_energy.clj" :var "compute-prediction-error"}
   :returns-record :prediction-error
   :writes [[:error {:record :prediction-error}]]}
  ;; WM-NODE-R7-I (WM-SUPERSET-D section 3): R3a -> R7 and R7 -> R3.
  ;; precision/weighted-error reads the prediction-error record's :error,
  ;; (:error error-map 0.0) (error-map aliased to :prediction-error; note
  ;; the 0.0 default the read supplies for a missing :error, which the
  ;; typed record's :present branch always carries), and returns (assoc
  ;; error-map :precision ... :weighted-error ...), the R7 re-weighting.
  ;; Its :weighted-error is declared unscoped: compute-prediction-error's
  ;; own :weighted-error sits in the :prediction-error record (attributed
  ;; there, undeclared), and the reader, belief/r3d-aggregate-driver, reads
  ;; (:weighted-error %) off classify-channel-entry's verdict records, which
  ;; copy the value from the R7 map through aggregate-member's (get err-map
  ;; k), k drawn from [:weighted-error :precision]. So the value reaches R3
  ;; by a copy the prover cannot follow key-for-key; the declared wire names
  ;; the key at both ends. r3-aggregate-driver is WM-SUPERSET-D section 4's
  ;; box (R3's packet by the discovery's rule, an edge in its later
  ;; endpoint's packet); created here at claude-8's direction so R7 -> R3 is
  ;; declared now, and R3's packet adds only its other boxes
  {:box/id :r7-weighted-error :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/precision.clj" :var "weighted-error"}
   :record-aliases {:prediction-error ["error-map"]}
   :reads [[:error {:record :prediction-error}]]
   :writes [:weighted-error]}
  {:box/id :r3-aggregate-driver :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/belief.clj" :var "r3d-aggregate-driver"}
   ;; WM-NODE-R3-I (WM-SUPERSET-D section 4): returns the typed driver
   ;; record, (assoc base :status :present :driver ...) in its cond
   ;; branches; :driver scoped to that record (:r3d-driver), read by judge
   :returns-record :r3d-driver
   :reads [:weighted-error] :writes [[:driver {:record :r3d-driver}]]}
  ;; WM-NODE-R3-I: R3's update and the morning-brief fold.
  ;; r3-apply-belief-events (war_machine/apply-arena-belief-events) forwards
  ;; belief-state and events positionally to belief/update-belief-batch; no
  ;; keyed field at either end (the belief's entity ids are read under a
  ;; variable key), so none is declared. morning-brief-fold
  ;; (war_machine/apply-morning-brief-events) returns {:belief ... :applied
  ;; ... :held ... :consumed-ids ...}; its :belief (scoped to the fold) is
  ;; read by judge as (:belief morning-brief-fold), E1's keyed hop b.
  ;; R3a -> R3 (eps) is a composition through R7 (:error into
  ;; weighted-error, :weighted-error into the driver); the join credits no
  ;; composition, so it stays on the record as such. E1 (R1 -> R3) and E2
  ;; (R3 -> R1) are R1's packet: E2's :passes, (:mu-post prev-trace-record)
  ;; into belief/reconcile-belief-carry arg 2, needs its callee box
  ;; r1-belief-carry (WM-SUPERSET-D section 5), which does not exist yet;
  ;; E1's sits on R1's box too
  {:box/id :r3-apply-belief-events :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj" :var "apply-arena-belief-events"}
   ;; WM-NODE-R1-I: E1's callee (belief-state, arg 1)
   :reads [:loop-belief]}
  ;; WM-NODE-R1-I (WM-SUPERSET-D section 5): R1's carry and the trace.
  ;; r1-belief-carry (belief/reconcile-belief-carry, R1's registry var)
  ;; takes [fresh-bootstrap carried-mu-post], plain parameters, and returns a
  ;; map keyed by entity id (read under a variable key): E2's callee, no
  ;; keyed field. trace-record (trace.clj) returns the v1 trace literal
  ;; (under a trailing cond->) with :mu-post (:belief judge-output), read by
  ;; the next tick's judge as (:mu-post prev-trace-record). Its own read of
  ;; judge's output :belief is not declared: judge's returned literal would
  ;; need :returns-record on the judge site, which would attribute every key
  ;; of judge's return to that record for every judge box
  {:box/id :r1-belief-carry :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/belief.clj" :var "reconcile-belief-carry"}
   :reads [:carried-mu-post]}
  {:box/id :trace-record :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/trace.clj" :var "trace-record"}
   :returns-record :trace
   :writes [[:mu-post {:record :trace}]]}
  {:box/id :morning-brief-fold :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj" :var "apply-morning-brief-events"}
   :returns-record :morning-brief-fold
   :writes [[:belief {:record :morning-brief-fold}]]}
  ;; WM-HANDOFF-H3-I (WM-HANDOFFS-D H3): the wants carry C, the read
  ;; criteria, from the flight into the tick. flight/click-wants (a defn)
  ;; builds {:wants :source :locators :universe} from the want source's
  ;; read-backs and the carried wants; flight/judge-opts puts :wants
  ;; :locators :universe under the click's :flight (a carrier: it reads them
  ;; and re-emits the same keys, so it is declared a reader and its writes
  ;; stand); http-click-fn posts (:flight judge-opts) as :flight-edn; in the
  ;; tick, judge hands (:flight judge-opts) to war_machine
  ;; flight-assembly-input, which reads them and writes them into the
  ;; assembly's :sources (:wants/:locators/:universes of the target), which
  ;; cascade_problems/assemble-one reads for the problem's :want (that next
  ;; hop, the sources map, has other writers and is not declared here). ONE
  ;; WRITER: click-wants for :wants and :universe. :locators is NOT declared
  ;; on these boxes: the key's one writer is the store entry's
  ;; (:r2-store-locators, H2), and the prover has no per-record scope, so
  ;; the wants' :locators is an undeclared kind of this carrier
  {:box/id :flight-click-wants :row 2 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/flight.clj" :var "click-wants"}
   :writes [:wants :universe]}
  {:box/id :flight-judge-opts :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/flight.clj" :var "judge-opts"}
   ;; WM-HANDOFF-H9+H11-I: (:target flight), scoped
   :reads [:wants :universe [:target {:record :flight}]]}
  {:box/id :tick-flight-assembly :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj" :var "flight-assembly-input"}
   ;; WM-HANDOFF-H5-I: writes the target's :universes (the flight's
   ;; :universe merged over the declared sources'), read by assemble-one.
   ;; WM-HANDOFF-H8-I: writes the sources' :wants of the flight's target
   ;; ((assoc-in [:sources :wants target] (vec (:wants flight)))), scoped to
   ;; the record :sources (WM-PROVER-RECORD-SCOPE-I, futon3c 5e4d9d02), so
   ;; it is a different vertex from the click's :wants it reads
   ;; WM-HANDOFF-H9+H11-I: (:target flight) keys the sources' entries
   :reads [:wants :universe [:target {:record :flight}]] :writes [:universes [:wants {:record :sources}]]}
  ;; WM-HANDOFF-H4-I (WM-HANDOFFS-D H4): the ask's answers reach
  ;; construction as the sources' :interpretations. publish! writes a
  ;; validated answer into the store under :patterns/:receipts (no
  ;; :interpretations key); want_interpretation/merge-published reads the
  ;; store back and writes the target's :interpretations into the sources,
  ;; called by the tick (war_machine assemble-cascade-problems-with-published)
  ;; and by the flight's view (flight_runner/target-view); in construction,
  ;; cascade_problems/assemble-one reads (get-in sources [:interpretations
  ;; target]) for the problem, and constructed-from-interpretations hands the
  ;; patterns and receipts to interpretation_construction/construct, which
  ;; reads :interpretations (destructured). ONE DECLARED WRITER:
  ;; merge-published, of the two textual writes in want_interpretation.clj.
  ;; The other, validate-response's assoc-in (:272), is a trial sources map
  ;; validate-response builds and assembles itself (cp/assemble) to check
  ;; the answer constructs; it never leaves the function, so the field does
  ;; not split there. Corrected at H5: two more writers of the sources'
  ;; :interpretations run earlier in the same judge, unboxed:
  ;; cascade_sources/load-declared (a declaration's patterns) and
  ;; mission_hole_wants/merge-into-sources (a mission hole's); merge-published
  ;; merges the store over them (a hand-written declaration wins on a
  ;; pattern id). The map models the ask's path, not the only writer. target-view is not boxed: its
  ;; form holds no :interpretations (it calls merge-published). enact-fn's
  ;; :interpretations is its opts' function over the store's :patterns
  ;; (flight_driver), not the sources' key, so :r0-enact-step does not
  ;; declare it (standing below)
  {:box/id :ask-merge-published :row 3 :box/kind :component
   :site {:file "futon2/src/futon2/aif/want_interpretation.clj" :var "merge-published"}
   :writes [:interpretations]}
  ;; WM-HANDOFF-H5-I (WM-HANDOFFS-D H5): the target's observed universe
  ;; into construction. flight-assembly-input (:tick-flight-assembly) merges
  ;; the flight's :universe into (get-in sources [:universes target]);
  ;; assemble-one reads it as the problem's :facts and hands it to
  ;; constructed-from-interpretations (positionally, as universe), which
  ;; gives construct its :observation. construct does not read :universes.
  ;; ONE DECLARED WRITER, flight-assembly-input, on the flight's path; two
  ;; more writers of the sources' :universes run earlier in the same judge,
  ;; unboxed: cascade_sources/load-declared and
  ;; mission_hole_wants/merge-into-sources. flight-assembly-input's merge is
  ;; the last, so for the flight's target a token the flight located wins
  ;; and a declared token it did not locate survives. WM-HANDOFF-H8-I: the
  ;; sources' wants, scoped [:wants {:record :sources}] (a vertex apart from
  ;; the click's :wants, which :flight-click-wants writes): written by
  ;; flight-assembly-input, read here by (get-in sources [:wants target]) as
  ;; the problem's :want, which is where C enters the problem (the
  ;; registry's R19 -> R5). The same two earlier writers of the sources'
